# Trivy ignores for The Bear Cave.
#
# Two kinds of entries live here:
#   - IaC misconfiguration check IDs (e.g. DS-0002), enforced by the
#     `trivy-config` job in .github/workflows/trivy-scan.yml.
#   - CVE vulnerability IDs, honored by the `scan` job's image scans
#     (trivy image auto-loads a repo-root .trivyignore with no flag).
#
# Entries here are CURRENT known-deferred findings only — if you remove one,
# CI starts failing on that check again, which is the point. Keep each line to
# the format "<ID> # <reason + tracking item>".

# IaC: services/nzbdav-exporter/Dockerfile runs as root (no USER directive).
# Deferred to improvement item 6 (Tier 3: non-root USER work).
DS-0002 # deferred: nzbdav-exporter non-root USER, item 6 / Tier 3

# ── Image CRITICAL CVEs (deferred) ────────────────────────────────────────────

# watchstate (ghcr.io/arabcoders/watchstate:latest, v1.10.3): Debian bookworm
# base packages with no fixed version published yet. Track: Debian bookworm
# point releases — libxml2 CVE-2026-6653, perl-base CVE-2026-13221/42496/8376.
# Re-check at every image update; remove each entry once upstream ships a fix.
CVE-2026-6653 # watchstate libxml2 DoS — no Debian fix yet
CVE-2026-13221 # watchstate perl-base regex — no Debian fix yet
CVE-2026-42496 # watchstate perl-base — no Debian fix yet
CVE-2026-8376 # watchstate perl-base — no Debian fix yet

# seerr (ghcr.io/seerr-team/seerr, v3.4.1): npm deps pinned in the upstream
# image (handlebars 4.7.8, tar 6.2.x). Fixed versions exist upstream
# (handlebars 4.7.9, tar 7.5.19) but the seerr image has not been rebuilt.
# Track: seerr-team/seerr releases — remove once the image is rebuilt.
CVE-2026-33937 # seerr handlebars RCE — upstream image needs rebuild
CVE-2026-59873 # seerr node-tar DoS — upstream image needs rebuild

# unpackerr (golift/unpackerr stable 0.15.2): alpine openssl stack with a
# published fix (3.5.6-r0) but the stable image hasn't been rebuilt since
# 2026-03-08. The unstable tag is unusable (binary ships mode 644). Track:
# golift/unpackerr stable rebuild — remove once the image is refreshed.
CVE-2026-31789 # unpackerr alpine openssl — stable image needs rebuild

# komga (gotson/komga:1.x): trivy reports Go stdlib v1.17.8 with 4 fixable
# CRITICALs (CVE-2023-24538/24540, CVE-2024-24790, CVE-2025-68121) but the
# image ships NO Go runtime/binary — Rust coreutils + komga.jar only (verified
# via ELF scan of every executable, 2026-08-28). Scan artifacts from the
# multi-stage build layers, not deployed code. Track: re-scan at deploy; remove
# if a future base actually bundles a Go toolchain.
CVE-2023-24538 # komga Go stdlib — no Go binary ships (scan artifact)
CVE-2023-24540 # komga Go stdlib — no Go binary ships (scan artifact)
CVE-2024-24790 # komga Go stdlib — no Go binary ships (scan artifact)
CVE-2025-68121 # komga Go stdlib — no Go binary ships (scan artifact)
